! HABM [m#2/s]: Heat conductivity Anomalous by Taroni for L-mode
! BOHM=c*Te/(e*B)=TE/BTOR*10^3[m^2/s]
! HABM=A_e*BOHM*q^2*(dp/dr)*a/p;
!  A_e recommended = 2.5E-4 is included in YHABM
!  Source: M.Erba et al. JET-R(95)02
!   (Pereverzev 04-AUG-95)
!  According to M.Erba et al. JET-P(96)10
!  a*(dp/dr)/p is replaced with a*(dp_e/dr)/p_e
!   (Pereverzev 31-MAR-98)
!  Dif ference with HATL in ABC <-> ROC
! Usage:  HE=HABM+HAGB+...
! Usage:  XI=2*HABM+HAGB+...
!
if ( J .eq. 1 ) then
 YLP = 0.
 YHABM = 0.5*ABC/HRO/BTOR
else
    YLP = YHABM*abs(NE(J)*TE(J)-NE(J-1)*TE(J-1))/(NE(J)+NE(J-1))
endif 
HABM = YLP/MU(J)**2
